  "description": "A parametric WASHBASIN on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE BOWL IS AN ELLIPSE cut into a rectangular counter, and the two are separate pieces — so a vanity top and its basin size independently, and the plan reads as a basin rather than a box with a circle drawn on it. The ring is built once and serves as both the plan outline and the mprism solid.\n\nTHREE SUPPORTS on one ternary: a Pedestal column, nothing at all for Wall-hung, or a full-width Vanity carcass set back from the front edge with a toe recess. Counter, bowl and tap are unchanged across all three.\n\nTHE TAP IS A REAL PIECE, not a line — a post standing above the rim at the back, on its own slot and colour, so it switches off for a basin taking a wall mixer.",
